7. RELIABILITY / ATTENUATION at n=685
==============================================================================
  respondents per country (manifest):        685
  median n_valid per item-country cell:      675
  median pooled N per item (30 countries):   20156

  median country-mean reliability, human:    0.9897
  median country-mean reliability, silicon:  0.9416
  median attenuation factor on r_bc:         0.9667  (3.3% attenuation)
  items with silicon-side reliability < .50: 2  ['hmsfmlsh', 'rlgatnd']
  items with human-side reliability < .50:   0

  r detectable at 80% power, WITHIN one country (n=675): 0.1077
  r detectable at 80% power, POOLED within-country (N=20156): 0.0197
  observed mean r_wc (per country-item cell):  +0.0271  (SD 0.0792)
  observed median r_pw (pooled within-country): +0.0429
  -> ABOVE the pooled threshold: the near-zero is estimated precisely, not merely undetected

  REPORTING RULE. The within-country figure alone cannot support a
  'genuine near-zero' claim, because the observed value lies below its
  own detection threshold. Quote the pooled comparison for that claim,
  and quote the within-country threshold only to say that no single
  country's estimate is individually informative. Note also that a
  larger sample cannot rescue the aggregate conclusions: the median
  attenuation on r_bc is only a few per cent.

